  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington is tracking ahead of last month on a calendar-adjusted basis \u2014 you're $85.6K MTD against an expected $87.4K, a real 2% miss, but that's tightly banded and driven entirely by a 17% drop in core grooming revenue yesterday. You had six groomers producing $508 per groomer (above your $498 trailing baseline), so the team performed, but you were down one groomer relative to last Wednesday's implied staffing. That's a capacity call, not execution. The bright spot: retail climbed 11% and transaction count is up week-to-date despite the dip \u2014 front-of-house is moving product. Year-to-date you're up 47% appointments and 47% revenue versus 2025; that's the real story. One leading indicator to watch closely: your 12+ week visit-gap bucket is shrinking (15.5% down to 13.3%), which signals retention is recovering.\n\nHicksville is outperforming expectations. You're $30.5K MTD against an expected $28.4K \u2014 a real +7.3% beat on a DOW-adjusted basis. Yesterday's 18% revenue lift and 19% grooming jump came off just three groomers at $458 per groomer (well above your $417 baseline), and your team sustained that without add-on attach softening meaningfully. The warning: your 12+ week bucket is growing (10.2% to 12.6%), a leading indicator of customer stretch-out. You have a reactivation opportunity in your lapse pool ($61.7K annual value), but the trend suggests you need to tighten retention focus there.\n\nBoth stores show inventory stress on bestsellers (X-Small Treat Table at -139 at Hicksville, -47 at Port Washington for Shanti's Medical Journey). Reorder now.\n\n**Today: 9 total groomer-days across both locations (6 Port Washington, 3 Hicksville) with 7.0 bather hours at Port Washington and zero at Hicksville; next 7 days: 49 groomer-days scheduled.**"
